{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_bdb2e1c3a3e6657118bbd3eb", "claim_ids": ["claim_43b5d16a9dc17c0963f1ba04", "claim_82444ab13528c083f9410825"], "query_ids": ["q_425"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_43b5d16a9dc17c0963f1ba04", "quote": "imports from Australia will be subject to a tariff of 12.5 per cent, along with 37 other economies.", "url": "https://www.dfat.gov.au/trade/trade-and-investment/latest-us-tariffs", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "12.5 per cent"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_82444ab13528c083f9410825", "quote": "The tariff edict states that copper, pharmaceuticals, semiconductors, bullion, and lumber articles will be exempt, as well as “energy and other certain minerals that are not available in the United States”, which is likely to include a range of critical minerals and uranium.", "url": "https://minerals.org.au/resources/us-tariffs-hurt-exporters-and-us-consumers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"affected_product": "copper, pharmaceuticals, semiconductors, bullion, and lumber articles"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_a38f7b00d8139788465f38f5", "claim_ids": ["claim_54cdb376dcd8ab5050d259a6", "claim_82444ab13528c083f9410825"], "query_ids": ["q_425"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_54cdb376dcd8ab5050d259a6", "quote": "While the baseline tariff on Australian exports is across the board, certain minerals may be exempt, with further clarification from the Trump Administration required.", "url": "https://minerals.org.au/resources/us-tariffs-hurt-exporters-and-us-consumers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "baseline tariff on Australian exports"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_82444ab13528c083f9410825", "quote": "The tariff edict states that copper, pharmaceuticals, semiconductors, bullion, and lumber articles will be exempt, as well as “energy and other certain minerals that are not available in the United States”, which is likely to include a range of critical minerals and uranium.", "url": "https://minerals.org.au/resources/us-tariffs-hurt-exporters-and-us-consumers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"affected_product": "copper, pharmaceuticals, semiconductors, bullion, and lumber articles"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_3f182193ac04ec26c9eb1b34", "claim_ids": ["claim_0ac71b6484ba7b50a9e5d359", "claim_2889c8a28d25adb516e414cb"], "query_ids": ["q_426"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_0ac71b6484ba7b50a9e5d359", "quote": "Canada recently agreed to match U.S. tariffs on Chinese EVs.", "url": "https://www.brookings.edu/articles/establishing-a-critical-minerals-club-across-north-america", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "match U.S. tariffs on Chinese EVs"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_2889c8a28d25adb516e414cb", "quote": "For example, Canada recently agreed to match U.S. tariffs on Chinese EVs.", "url": "https://www.brookings.edu/articles/establishing-a-critical-minerals-club-across-north-america", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"exporting_country": "Canada"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_b3e62fa15089aa055a51cdf0", "claim_ids": ["claim_34195352033d011edacb9771", "claim_7826fd76a2294c945041d18a"], "query_ids": ["q_426"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_34195352033d011edacb9771", "quote": "Washington responded by imposing 50% tariffs on roughly US$20 billion worth of Canadian goods, including autos, parts and steel.", "url": "https://mexicobusiness.news/mining/news/us-canada-trade-war-ontario-cut-electricity-minerals", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "50% tariffs", "affected_product": "autos, parts and steel"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_7826fd76a2294c945041d18a", "quote": "The framework under negotiation before talks collapsed would have cut US auto tariffs on Canada from 25% to 15% and steel and aluminum duties from 50% to 25%", "url": "https://mexicobusiness.news/mining/news/us-canada-trade-war-ontario-cut-electricity-minerals", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "cut US auto tariffs on Canada from 25% to 15% and steel and aluminum duties from 50% to 25%"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_82920bb1c71cc38f1c626109", "claim_ids": ["claim_695bf72418b1378b03bd72b5", "claim_729a8c9db920b5dc2434d4c1"], "query_ids": ["q_427"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_695bf72418b1378b03bd72b5", "quote": "On August 4, 2026, the Bureau of Industry and Security filed a temporary final rule with the Federal Register that implements one of the most consequential single regulatory actions the US battery recycling industry has ever faced. The black mass export restrictions take effect on August 27, 2026, twenty-one days after publication, and require U.S. persons engaged in the sale of black mass to allocate 100 percent of monthly sales to U.S. persons unless the Bureau grants a case-by-case exception.", "url": "https://www.greenli-ion.com/post/bis-black-mass-export-restrictions-directive-allocation-order", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "black mass export restrictions", "legal_authority": "Defense Priorities and Allocations System at 15 CFR Part 700 to issue a Directive Allocation Order", "effective_date": "August 27, 2026", "reported_policy_status": "temporary final rule"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_729a8c9db920b5dc2434d4c1", "quote": "The export prohibition—expressed as a “100% domestic sales requirement”—takes effect on August 27, 2026, and is expected to remain effective for at least one year.", "url": "https://www.bdlaw.com/publications/new-u-s-restrictions-on-export-of-black-mass-from-recycling-lithium-ion-batteries-pose-major-challenges-for-battery-recycling", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"effective_date": "August 27, 2026"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_077cb7a06882a4694821f02a", "claim_ids": ["claim_a6012f2fa808268fff611596", "claim_bcd14343c905225842441477"], "query_ids": ["q_427"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_a6012f2fa808268fff611596", "quote": "On August 6, 2026, the Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS) within the U.S. Department of Commerce issued a “Temporary Final Rule” prohibiting exports of two materials—black mass from the initial stage of recycling lithium-ion batteries (LIBs) and tungsten waste and scrap—without a license, adjustment, or exception issued by BIS.", "url": "https://www.bdlaw.com/publications/new-u-s-restrictions-on-export-of-black-mass-from-recycling-lithium-ion-batteries-pose-major-challenges-for-battery-recycling", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Temporary Final Rule", "legal_authority": "Defense Production Act", "affected_product": "black mass from the initial stage of recycling lithium-ion batteries (LIBs)", "announcement_date": "August 6, 2026", "effective_date": "August 27, 2026"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_bcd14343c905225842441477", "quote": "starting [INSERT 21 DAYS AFTER DATE OF PUBLICATION IN THE FEDERAL REGISTER], U.S. persons engaged in the sale of black mass (Schedule B codes 8549.13.00.00, 8549.14.00.00, and 8549.19.00.00) and tungsten waste and scrap (Schedule B code 8101.97.00.00) must allocate 100 percent of monthly sales to U.S. persons", "url": "https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-16078.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_818d5d4bd4a6eeef1896cfc9", "claim_ids": ["claim_afce45c44fe75fbac7bfe5b7", "claim_b2f26f5ef84491fdf86bf0ec"], "query_ids": ["q_428"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_afce45c44fe75fbac7bfe5b7", "quote": "Trump imposed 25 percent tariffs on Korean imports in April, before placing them on a 90-day pause. If South Korea were to implement retaliatory tariffs in response, it could cut off a key revenue stream for the U.S. industry.", "url": "https://grist.org/technology/trump-battery-recycling-lithium-grants-funding-tariffs-ira-tax-credits", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "25 percent"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_b2f26f5ef84491fdf86bf0ec", "quote": "Trump imposed 25 percent tariffs on Korean imports in April, before placing them on a 90-day pause.", "url": "https://grist.org/technology/trump-battery-recycling-lithium-grants-funding-tariffs-ira-tax-credits", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "25 percent tariffs", "duty_rate": "25 percent"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_c38c85110aba421ca86feb51", "claim_ids": ["claim_2d2d596abd8b094a01eed9c1", "claim_b2d23a9a1a245dab5042abc0"], "query_ids": ["q_429"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_2d2d596abd8b094a01eed9c1", "quote": "In 2021, the U.S. Secretary of Commerce launched an investigation of the effects of imports of NdFeB magnets on National Security to evaluate whether Section 232 of the Trade Expansion Act of 1962 is applicable for addressing the issues in the supply chain.", "url": "https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2022-02/Neodymium%20Magnets%20Supply%20Chain%20Report%20-%20Final.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 232 of the Trade Expansion Act of 1962", "legal_authority": "U.S. Secretary of Commerce launched an investigation", "announcement_date": "2021"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_b2d23a9a1a245dab5042abc0", "quote": "In 2021, the U.S. Secretary of Commerce launched an investigation of the effects of imports of NdFeB magnets on National Security to evaluate whether Sec tion 232 of the Trade Expansion Act of 1962 is applicable for addressing the issues in the supply chain.", "url": "https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2022-02/Neodymium%20Magnets%20Supply%20Chain%20Report%20-%20Final.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "U.S. Secretary of Commerce launched an investigation", "affected_product": "NdFeB magnets", "announcement_date": "2021"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_0c35ed5be04c39083708899c", "claim_ids": ["claim_32e90975c9d19ff6061ecfa1", "claim_4f1ba4e9528ed8afc586a25d"], "query_ids": ["q_429"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_32e90975c9d19ff6061ecfa1", "quote": "MP Materials recently announced plans to construct a magnet production facility in Fort Wo rth, Texas, to supply NdFeB magnets to General Motors (GM) for use in its vehicles.", "url": "https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2022-02/Neodymium%20Magnets%20Supply%20Chain%20Report%20-%20Final.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "MP Materials", "facility": "Fort Wo rth, Texas"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_4f1ba4e9528ed8afc586a25d", "quote": "Rare earth materials sourced from Mountain Pass, California, will be manufactured into magnets at new MP Materials production facility in Fort Worth, Texas", "url": "https://mpmaterials.com/news//general-motors-and-mp-materials-enter-long-term-supply-agreement-to-scale-rare-earth-magnet-sourcing-and-production-in-the-us", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "MP Materials"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_09229cb96cbab6cbba119c51", "claim_ids": ["claim_378536b8745601b6c6ff5c32", "claim_d212e735bf88fd46b646dbf2"], "query_ids": ["q_429"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_378536b8745601b6c6ff5c32", "quote": "Quadrant also recently announced plans to begin producing magnets in the U.S., with initial target production capacity of 1,500 -2,000 tonnes/year in 2024.", "url": "https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2022-02/Neodymium%20Magnets%20Supply%20Chain%20Report%20-%20Final.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Quadrant"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_d212e735bf88fd46b646dbf2", "quote": "Quadrant also recently announced plans to begin producing magnets in the U.S., with initial target production capacity of 1,500 -2,000 tonnes/year in 2024.", "url": "https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2022-02/Neodymium%20Magnets%20Supply%20Chain%20Report%20-%20Final.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Quadrant"}}]}]}

